issues.description:
CLI tool to detect and fix discrepancies between local database state and external processor state (NMI/Mobius, CCBill)

## Metadata

- Category: tooling
- Status: not_started
- Passes: false

## Details

- ccbill_datalink: {"description":"CCBill DataLink provides SFTP/API access to batch export files","data_available":["Subscription transactions (new, rebill, cancel, expire, chargeback)","Consumer info (partial - for support lookups)","Daily/weekly/monthly batch files"],"sync_flow":["1. Fetch DataLink export for date range","2. Parse transactions by type","3. For each transaction, check if we have matching record","4. Flag discrepancies (missing records, status mismatches)"],"existing_code":"internal/integrations/ccbill/datalink.go exists but may be incomplete"}
- cli_design: {"command":"billing-cli processor-sync","subcommands":["billing-cli processor-sync check - find discrepancies (dry run)","billing-cli processor-sync fix - find and fix discrepancies","billing-cli processor-sync report - generate detailed report"],"flags":["--processor=ccbill|nmi|all - which processor(s) to check","--since=DATE - start date for checking","--until=DATE - end date for checking (default: now)","--user=USER_ID - check specific user only","--subscription=SUB_ID - check specific subscription only","--format=table|json|csv - output format","--dry-run - show what would be fixed without making changes","--auto-fix - automatically fix safe discrepancies","--output=FILE - write report to file"]}
- context: {"problem":"Our database may drift out of sync with processor records due to missed webhooks, failed processing, network issues, or bugs","data_sources":{"ccbill":"DataLink API - provides batch export of subscription and transaction data","nmi":"Transaction Query API and Customer Vault Query API - query transactions and stored payment methods"},"use_cases":["Detect subscriptions in processor that we don't have locally","Detect subscriptions we have locally that processor cancelled/expired","Find payments we missed (charged but no Payment record)","Find chargebacks/refunds we didn't process","Reconcile payment method/vault status"]}
- discrepancy_types: [{"id":"PS-1","name":"processor_subscription_not_local","description":"Subscription exists at processor but not in our database","severity":"CRITICAL","action":"Create local subscription record or investigate orphan at processor"},{"id":"PS-2","name":"local_subscription_not_at_processor","description":"We have an active subscription but processor shows cancelled/expired","severity":"HIGH","action":"Update local status to match processor"},{"id":"PS-3","name":"status_mismatch","description":"Local status differs from processor status (e.g., we show active, they show past_due)","severity":"MEDIUM","action":"Reconcile to processor's status (source of truth)"},{"id":"PS-4","name":"payment_missing_locally","description":"Processor has successful charge but no Payment record locally","severity":"HIGH","action":"Create Payment record and grant entitlements if needed"},{"id":"PS-5","name":"refund_not_processed","description":"Processor shows refund but no refund record locally","severity":"HIGH","action":"Create refund record, revoke entitlements if appropriate"},{"id":"PS-6","name":"chargeback_not_processed","description":"Processor shows chargeback but subscription still active locally","severity":"CRITICAL","action":"Terminate subscription, revoke entitlements"},{"id":"PS-7","name":"payment_method_vault_mismatch","description":"Local payment method record differs from processor vault (wrong card, inactive)","severity":"MEDIUM","action":"Update local record to match processor"}]
- fix_actions: {"auto_fixable":["PS-2: Update local status to match processor","PS-3: Update local status to match processor","PS-7: Update local payment method record"],"requires_manual_review":["PS-1: Orphan processor subscription needs investigation","PS-4: Missing payment needs entitlement check","PS-5: Refund may need entitlement revocation decision","PS-6: Chargeback needs entitlement revocation"]}
- nmi_batch_api: {"description":"NMI Query API allows transaction and subscription lookup","endpoints":["GET transactions - query by date range, customer, subscription","GET customers - query customer vault records","GET recurring - query subscription status"],"sync_flow":["1. Query NMI for transactions in date range","2. Query NMI for active/cancelled subscriptions","3. Compare with local subscription/payment records","4. Flag discrepancies"]}

Accept credit card details directly on our server instead of proxying through Mobius/NMI's hosted tokenization

## Metadata

- Category: architecture
- Priority: low
- Status: not_started
- Passes: false

## Details

- context: {"current_flow":["1. Frontend collects card info in Mobius-hosted iframe/form","2. Card data sent directly to Mobius/NMI (never touches our server)","3. Mobius returns a payment token or customer_vault_id","4. Our server uses token to charge via NMI API"],"proposed_flow":["1. Frontend collects card info in our own form","2. Card data POSTed to our server","3. Our server sends card data directly to NMI API","4. Store customer_vault_id for future charges"],"why_consider":["Full control over checkout UX (no iframe styling limitations)","Faster checkout (no redirect to third-party)","Can implement custom validation and error handling","Reduce dependency on Mobius-specific integration"]}
- nmi_api_parameters: {"direct_card_fields":["ccnumber - Credit card number","ccexp - Expiration date (MMYY format)","cvv - Card security code"],"with_customer_vault":["customer_vault=add_customer - Store card in vault","Returns customer_vault_id for future charges"]}
- pci_compliance_requirements: {"current_level":"SAQ A or SAQ A-EP (card data never touches our servers)","required_level":"SAQ D or full PCI DSS assessment","key_requirements":["Encrypt card data in transit (TLS 1.2+) - already done","Never store full card numbers (only last 4 + token)","Never log card data","Quarterly vulnerability scans by ASV (Approved Scanning Vendor)","Annual penetration testing","Secure coding practices audit","Network segmentation for cardholder data environment","Access controls and audit logging","Incident response plan"],"cost_estimate":{"asv_quarterly_scans":"$100-500/quarter","annual_pentest":"$5,000-20,000/year","pci_assessment":"$15,000-50,000/year for SAQ D","ongoing_compliance":"Significant engineering time for documentation and controls"}}
- recommendation: {"verdict":"Probably not worth it for current scale","reasoning":["PCI SAQ D compliance is expensive and time-consuming","Hosted tokenization (current approach) is industry standard","Mobius iframe can be styled reasonably well","Security risk/liability not worth UX improvement"],"reconsider_when":["Processing >$1M/month and UX is measurably hurting conversion","Mobius hosted form has significant technical limitations","We hire dedicated security/compliance staff"]}
- risks: ["PCI compliance burden and ongoing costs","Security liability if breached (card data exposure)","Mobius may not support direct integration (contractual requirement for hosted form)","More attack surface on our servers"]
